            "body": ">  think the following diff results in an easier to understand code (and hopefully works on Windows):\r\n\r\nThanks! Yes, it's an improvement, but windows still fails:\r\n\r\n```make\r\nFAIL in tests\\test_sessions.lua | restart() | works when characters in session name have special meaning: nvim_exec2(), line 1: Vim(mksession):E190: Cannot open \"D:/a/mini.nvim/mini.nvim/tests/dir-sessions/empty/new/ /tests/dir-sessions/file!/ session\" for writing\r\n  Traceback:\r\n    tests\\test_sessions.lua:1072\r\n```",
