        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> ```makefile\r\n>     tests\\test_sessions.lua:1072\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nThat is the error from the test case code itself, not from `MiniSessions.restart()` implementation. The reason is that `make_path()` normalizes path (i.e. also replaces `\\` with `/` path separators on Windows). The `vim.fn.fnameescape` is applied too early (i.e. during path creation), when it should be usually applied as late as possible (just before constructing a command for `vim.cmd` / `child.cmd`).",
            "created_at": "2026-04-15T17:07:46Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/pull/2371#issuecomment-4253990330",
